Domain"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"nfc-identifiers-list.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a NFC Privacy description","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"orderedList","start":9,"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the “Privacy - NFC Usage Scan Description” key and a string that describes what you will use NFC for in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the application e.g “The application needs access to NFC reading to communicate with your YubiKey.”","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"nfc-privacy.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"SmartCardUSB","level":3,"text":"SmartCard\/USB"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To support YubiKeys connected via the USB port on a device running iOS 16 or higher, you need to add the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.apple.security.smartcard"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement to your application."}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Select the application entitlements file.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.smartcard","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement to the entitlement list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"smart-card.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"USB SmartCard supports Yubico OTP slot programming. HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response requires","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDOTPConnection"},{"text":" on macOS, ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/LightningSmartCardConnection","isActive":true},{"text":", or NFC without a touch requirement.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"LightningAccessoryConnection-ie-5Ci-YubiKey","level":3,"text":"Lightning\/AccessoryConnection i.e 5Ci YubiKey"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To add support for the 5Ci YubiKey that connect to the iPhone via the Lightning port you need to add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"type":"text","text":" string to the list of External Accessories."}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Select your project.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Select your application target.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Choose the “Info” tab.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If not present add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Supported external accessory protocols","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" key and insert the string ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.yubico.ylp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in its list.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"external-accessory.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The YubiKey 5Ci is an Apple MFi certified external accessory and communicates over iAP2. Setting the value for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Supported external accessory protocols"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"com.yubico.ylp"},{"text":" will tell the app that all communication with the 5Ci YubiKey via the Lightning port is done using the External Accessory framework.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Making-Your-First-Connection","level":2,"text":"Making Your First Connection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now that your project is configured, you can start connecting to YubiKeys. YubiKit provides different connection types depending on how the YubiKey is connected to the device."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Types","level":3,"text":"Understanding Connection Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YubiKit provides the following connection methods:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"NFC","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Short-range wireless communication (iOS only)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"USB","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Direct USB connection via SmartCard interface","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Lightning","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": YubiKey 5Ci connected to Lightning port (iOS only)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"USB HID","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Direct access to the FIDO or OTP interface (macOS only)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connection type works differently, so let’s explore how to use them."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"NFC-Connections","level":3,"text":"NFC Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC connections are user-initiated and short-lived. The user must bring their YubiKey close to their device:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Start an NFC scan","do {","    let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","","    \/\/ Use the connection quickly - NFC sessions have a timeout","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Always close NFC connections with a user message","    await connection.close(message: \"OATH codes retrieved\")","","} catch {","    \/\/ Handle connection errors (user cancelled, no YubiKey found, etc.)","    print(\"NFC connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"NFC connections automatically show the iOS NFC interface and require user interaction to complete."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"USB-and-Lightning-Connections","level":3,"text":"USB and Lightning Connections"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wired connections are persistent - they stay connected until the YubiKey is unplugged:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import YubiKit","","\/\/ Connect to any wired YubiKey (USB or Lightning)","do {","    let connection = try await WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()","","    \/\/ Perform operations - connection stays active","    let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","    let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","    \/\/ Monitor for disconnection or close when done","    let error = await connection.waitUntilClosed()","    if let error = error {","        print(\"Connection closed with error: \\(error)\")","    }","","} catch {","    print(\"Wired connection failed: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WiredSmartCardConnection.makeConnection()"},{"type":"text","text":" method automatically detects whether you’re using USB or Lightning."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Specific-Connection-Types","level":3,"text":"Specific Connection Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more control, you can connect to specific interfaces:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ USB only","let usbConnection = try await USBSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ Lightning only (iOS)","let lightningConnection = try await LightningSmartCardConnection()","","\/\/ NFC with custom message (iOS)","let nfcConnection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection(","    alertMessage: \"Hold your YubiKey near the phone\"",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On macOS, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDOTPConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" for the OTP keyboard interface or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDFIDOConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the FIDO interface:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let otpConnection = try await HIDOTPConnection()"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Understanding-Connection-Lifecycle","level":2,"text":"Understanding Connection Lifecycle"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Critical:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Connections must be explicitly closed. You can only have one active connection to a YubiKey at any time."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Connection-Behavior","level":3,"text":"Connection Behavior"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exclusive access","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Only one connection can exist per YubiKey at any time","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Manual closure required","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Dropping a connection reference does NOT automatically close it - you must call ","type":"text"},{"code":"close()","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Resource blocking","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": An unclosed connection prevents new connections (throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"SmartCardConnectionError.busy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each connection is a lightweight value type that identifies an active hardware session. Copying a connection creates another handle to the same session, not a new connection - the hardware is only released when you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"close()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Working-with-Sessions","level":2,"text":"Working with Sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you have a connection, create sessions to access different YubiKey applications:"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"OATH-Session-TOTPHOTP-codes","level":3,"text":"OATH Session (TOTP\/HOTP codes)"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let session = try await OATHSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let codes = try await session.calculateCredentialCodes()","","for (credential, code) in codes {","    print(\"\\(credential.label): \\(code?.code ?? \"Touch required\")\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Yubico-OTP-Session-OTP-slots","level":3,"text":"Yubico OTP Session (OTP slots)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" manages the two OTP slots. Create it with a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on macOS, an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OTPConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let session = try await YubiOTP.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","let state = await session.configState","print(\"Slot 2 configured: \\(try state.isConfigured(.two))\")","","\/\/ Program slot 2 for HOTP, replacing its existing configuration","try await session.putConfiguration(.hotp(key: secret), in: .two)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/YubiOTP\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for HMAC-SHA1 challenge-response, transport support, and NFC output."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"PIV-Session-Certificates-and-keys","level":3,"text":"PIV Session (Certificates and keys)"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let session = try await PIVSession.makeSession(connection: connection)","let certificate = try await session.getCertificate(in: .authentication)","print(\"Found certificate: \\(certificate.subject)\")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Management-Session-Device-information","level":3,"text":"Management Session (Device information)"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let session: Management.Session = try await .makeSession(connection: connection)","print(\"YubiKey version: \\(await session.version)\")","","let deviceInfo = try await session.getDeviceInfo()","print(\"Device info: \\(deviceInfo)\")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"WebAuthn-Client-FIDO2--passkeys","level":3,"text":"WebAuthn Client (FIDO2 \/ passkeys)"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For passkey registration and authentication, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" wraps a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and runs the W3C ceremonies end-to-end. CTAP2 sessions can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HIDFIDOConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" (USB HID on macOS) or any "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/SmartCardConnection","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(NFC \/ USB CCID)."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let connection = try await HIDFIDOConnection()","let session = try await CTAP2.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","","let client = WebAuthn.Client(","    session: session,","    origin: try .init(\"https:\/\/example.com\"),","    isPublicSuffix: { publicSuffixList.contains($0) }",")","","let response = try await client.makeCredential(","    .init(","        challenge: challenge,","        rp: .init(id: \"example.com\", name: \"Example\"),","        user: .init(id: userId, name: \"alice@example.com\")","    ),","    authorization: .pin(\"1234\")",").value"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PIN and UV are supplied per ceremony via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authorization","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". For raw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CTAP2 access (credential management, bio enrollment, large blobs), use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" directly."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Connection-Management-Patterns","level":2,"text":"Connection Management Patterns"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"For-UI-Applications","level":3,"text":"For UI Applications"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In SwiftUI or UIKit apps, you typically want to maintain persistent connections and react to connection changes. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OATHSampleCode","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for complete examples of reactive connection management pa